-- title:
--   Integrality of Y⁶jmatĥ⁴(jmatĥ-1728)³ over ℂ[jmatĥ]
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ of finite index, and assume that $1$ belongs to `strictPeriods` of the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb R)$, so that $q = e^{2\pi i\tau}$ serves as parameter at the cusp and $q$-expansions with respect to the period $1$ are available. Let $f$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ for that subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb R)$. Write $\hat\jmath =$ `coeffEmb ℂ jq` for the image in $\mathbb C((q))$, under the coefficientwise map induced by $\mathbb Q \to \mathbb C$, of the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot \mathtt{jNumQ}(q) \in \mathbb Q((q))$ (the rational $q$-expansion of the modular invariant), and let $\theta$ denote the $\mathbb C$-linear operator $g \mapsto q\,\mathrm d g/\mathrm d q$ on $\mathbb C((q))$, i.e. multiplication by the monomial $q$ after applying the formal derivative. Let $Y \in \mathbb C((q))$ satisfy $Y\cdot\theta(\hat\jmath) = \widehat f$, where $\widehat f$ is the $q$-expansion of $f$ at period $1$, viewed in $\mathbb C((q))$. Then $Y^6\,\hat\jmath^{\,4}\,(\hat\jmath - 1728)^3$ is integral over the $\mathbb C$-subalgebra of $\mathbb C((q))$ generated by $\hat\jmath$.
--
--   Since classically $\theta j = -E_4^2E_6/\Delta$, $j = E_4^3/\Delta$ and $j-1728 = E_6^2/\Delta$, the element in question is the $q$-expansion of $f^6/\Delta$, a modular function for $\Gamma$ holomorphic on the upper half-plane, and the assertion is the integrality of such functions over $\mathbb C[j]$ obtained by taking the norm down to level one. It is used in the analysis of regular differentials on the modular curve, via [`ModularCurve.mem_regularDifferentials_x1FunctionFieldBar_of_coeffMap_diffQExp_eq_qExpansion`](thm.html#ModularCurve.mem_regularDifferentials_x1FunctionFieldBar_of_coeffMap_diffQExp_eq_qExpansion); the proof cites the $q$-expansion identity [`ModularCurve.jqModC_eq_qExpansion_E4_cube_div_discriminant`](thm.html#ModularCurve.jqModC_eq_qExpansion_E4_cube_div_discriminant), the Rankin–Cohen bracket construction [`ModularForm.exists_rankinCohen_one_qExpansion_eq`](thm.html#ModularForm.exists_rankinCohen_one_qExpansion_eq), and the integrality statement [`ModularForm.isIntegral_adjoin_qExpansion_div_discriminant_pow_of_isArithmetic`](thm.html#ModularForm.isIntegral_adjoin_qExpansion_div_discriminant_pow_of_isArithmetic).
